
                DayDream BBS V1.01, DayDream.DAT Structure
                ------------------------------------------

OFFSET  TYPE     LENGTH  DESCRIPTION                                     FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0000   STRING     25    BOARD NAME                                        (-)
 0026   STRING     25    SYSOP NAME (SHOULD BE SAME AS IN YOUR ACCOUNT)    (-)
 0052   UBYTE	   01    CHAT MODE: 0 = LINE, 1 = SPLIT, 2 = ASK, 3 = DOOR (-)
 0053   UBYTE      01    LOCAL SCREEN LENGTH                               (-)
 0054	ULONG      04    USER DEFAULTS
 0058   FREE BLOCK 05    FREE SPACE RESERVED FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT        (-)
 0063   STRING     20    DEFAULT PATH FOR SYSOP'S ASCII SEND COMMAND       (-)
 0084   STRING     40    SYSTEM OPERATOR'S DOWNLOAD PATH (FOR CHAT XFERS)  (-)
 0125   BYTE       01    DISPLAY MODE ID TO BE USED IN OPERATOR LOGIN      (-)
 0126   ULONG      04    COPY BUFFER SIZE (BYTES)                          (-)
 0130   UBYTE      01    CONFERENCE TO JOIN IF AUTO-JOIN-CONF FAILS        (-)
 0131   STRING     10    COLOR FOR SYSOP IN CHAT                           (-)
 0142   STRING     10    COLOR FOR USER IN CHAT                            (-)
 0153   UBYTE      01    LINE ED CHARACTER                                 (-)
 0154   STRING     15    SYSTEM PASSWORD                                   (-)
 0170   STRING     15    NEW USER REGISTRATION PASSWORD                    (-)
 0186   STRING     15    ON-LINE USER EDITOR PASSWORD                      (-)
 0202   LONG WORD  04    NUMBER USED IN UNIQUE MESSAGE NUMBERING (++)      (-)
 0206   BYTE       01    FILE-DIRECTORY SCAN: BUFFER SIZE (KB)             (-)
 0207   BYTE       01    PRESET NUMBER TO SET FOR NEW USERS                (-)
 0208   LONG WORD  04    INACTIVITY TIMEOUT IN SECONDS                     (-)
 0212   LONG WORD  04    FREE BYTES IN HDD REQUIRED FOR UPLOADS            (-)
 0216   LONG WORD  04    SYSTEM FLAGS                                      (-)
 0220	STRING     15    SHELL PASSWORD                                    (-)
 0236	STRING	   39    PATH TO PLACE FILES IF THEY ARE ALIENS IN TEMP    (-)
 0276   STRING     70    FULL SCREEN EDITOR COMMAND                        (-)
 0347   STRING     99    FREE DOWNLOAD LINE                                (-)
 0447   STRING     40    PATH FOR OLMs                                     (-)
 0488   UBYTE      01    COSYSOP ACCESS LEVEL                              (-)
 0489   UBYTE      01    CONTROL CODE TO REPLACE (255)                     (-)
 0490   STRING     39    PATH FOR HOMEDIRECTORIES (INTERNET)               (-)
 0530   UWORD      02    GROUP ID FOR BBS USERS (INTERNET)                 (-)
 0532   UWORD      02    USER ID FOR FIRST ACCOUNT (INTERNET)              (-)
 0534   STRING     70    EXTERNAL CHATTER                                  (-)
 0605   BYTE       01    MAILSCAN TYPE                                     (-)
 0606   FREE BLOCK 3395  FREE SPACE RESERVED FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT        (-)
 4000   -- END --  00    END OF THE MAIN CONFIGURATION STRUCTURE           (-)
==============================================================================

BIT   MEANING WHEN SET AS PRESENTED BELOW                         SYSTEM FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0    0: DO NOT ASK CHAT REASON          1: ASK CHAT REASON
 1    0: REAL NAMES IN WHO ETC           1: HANDLES IN WHO ETC
 2    0: LOCATION IN WHO ETC             1: ORGANIZATION IN WHO ETC
 3    0: ENABLE WILDCARDS IN LOGON       1: DISABLE WILDCARDS IN LOGON
 4    0: QUESTIONAIRE ONLY FOR NEW USERS 1: ASK Q IF NOT ANSWERED YET
 5    0: ENABLE LOGWRITES FOR OPERATOR   1: DISABLE LOGWRITES FOR OPERATOR
 6    0: $ ENTERS COMMAND MODE IN MSG-ED 1: CR ENTERS COMMAND MODE IN MSGED
 7    0: ASK REAL NAME FIRST (NEW USERS) 1: ASK HANDLE FIRST
==============================================================================


BIT  0:MEANING                    1:MEANING                           DEFAULTS
==============================================================================
002  Do Not Hide Cursor           Hide Cursor For Faster Output
003  Regular Escape Sequence      Replace <ESC>[ With ASCII #155
004  Novice User Mode             Expert User Mode
005  Personal Mail Check ON       Personal Mail Check Off
006  New Files Scan Off           New Files Scan On
009  Allow nodemessages           Disallow nodemessages
010  CLS's in filelists	          No CLS's in filelists
011                               Ask FSEd/LineED
012                               Ask MailScan/NoMailScan
013                               Ask FileScan/NoFileScan
014                               Autoquick uploading
015  Background checker           Normal checker
==============================================================================
